CoworkEnv — source and third-party notices
========================================

The first release selects data-construction utilities from the project's
existing claw-adapters development tree. Original file hashes and release
changes are recorded in docs/source_manifest.json. The public snapshot is not
a full copy of that development tree or a reproduction of all its experiments.

Claw-Eval
---------
Upstream: https://github.com/claw-eval/claw-eval
License: MIT; copyright (c) 2026 claw-eval.
Full upstream notice: third_party/claw-eval.LICENSE.

data_construction/d1_catalog/*.json adapts tool and endpoint definitions from
Claw-Eval task interfaces, including project extensions. The generator emits
configuration and a grader that refer to Claw-Eval runtime APIs. The upstream
license was checked at https://github.com/claw-eval/claw-eval/blob/main/LICENSE
on 2026-10-20; older internal notes predate that available license.

The generator's service routes and grader signatures are an integration
contract, not a claim of compatibility with every upstream version. Service
servers, the Claw-Eval package, benchmark tasks/data and adapters are not
bundled. Their release/versioning and any additional terms remain separate.

Other dependencies
------------------
PyYAML is installed separately and is not vendored. The result reader accepts
Harbor-style result.json layouts; no Harbor runtime source is redistributed.
ClawMark, WildClawBench, Slime and Megatron code/data are not included in this
snapshot. References to future integrations do not grant rights to those
projects or imply that an integration has been released or validated.
